IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 6 OFFENCES AND PENALTIES: the sections and subsections not in sgta-part6-offences.l4: s 53(3), (4), (7); s 57(1), (2), (4) to (6);
-- s 58(1); ss 60 to 63; s 64(3), (4); ss 65 to 70.  (s 54, 55, 56, 59, 71 and the other subsections of ss 53, 57, 58, 64 are in
-- sgta-part6-offences.l4; s 85, the general penalty where a section states none, is in sgta-part8-penalties.l4.)
-- Seat: the accused person, and the person whose thing is seized.  Where a section states no penalty, the general penalty of s 85 applies.

§ `s 53(3), (4), (7): who is guilty, and the notice that the defence needs`

-- src:4851 | (3) In the case of an offence in relation to a telecommunication
-- src:4852 | system or service not extending beyond Singapore, the person or
-- src:4853 | every person operating the system or service (or, if different people
-- src:4854 | run different parts of the system or service, each of them) shall be
-- src:4855 | guilty of an offence and shall be similarly liable.
@ref s 53(3) (src:4851-4855)
GIVEN `the offence is in relation to a telecommunication system or service not extending beyond Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person or one of the persons operating the system or service, or operates a part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(3): the person is guilty of an offence and similarly liable` MEANS
    `the offence is in relation to a telecommunication system or service not extending beyond Singapore` AND `the person is the person or one of the persons operating the system or service, or operates a part of it`

-- src:4857 | (4) In the case of an offence in relation to a telecommunication
-- src:4858 | system or service extending beyond Singapore, the person or every
-- src:4859 | person operating that portion of such system or service within
-- src:4860 | Singapore (or, if different people operate different parts of the system
-- src:4861 | or service, each of them) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:4862 | similarly liable.
@ref s 53(4) (src:4857-4862)
GIVEN `the offence is in relation to a telecommunication system or service extending beyond Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person or one of the persons operating that portion of the system or service within Singapore, or operates a part of it within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(4): the person is guilty of an offence and similarly liable` MEANS
    `the offence is in relation to a telecommunication system or service extending beyond Singapore` AND `the person is the person or one of the persons operating that portion of the system or service within Singapore, or operates a part of it within Singapore`

-- src:4875 | (7) Where the defence provided by subsection (6) involves an
-- src:4876 | allegation that the commission of the offence was due to the act or
-- src:4877 | default of another person, the person charged is not, without
-- src:4878 | permission of the court, entitled to rely on that defence unless,
-- src:4879 | within a period ending 7 clear days before the hearing, the person
-- src:4880 | charged has served on the prosecutor a written notice giving such
-- src:4881 | information identifying or assisting in the identification of that other
-- src:4882 | person as was then in the possession of the person charged.
@ref s 53(7) (src:4875-4882)
GIVEN `the defence under subsection (6) involves an allegation that the offence was due to the act or default of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days before the hearing, ending 7 clear days before, by which the person charged served on the prosecutor a written notice identifying or assisting in the identification of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(7): the person charged may rely on the defence under subsection (6)` MEANS
    (NOT `the defence under subsection (6) involves an allegation that the offence was due to the act or default of another person`)
    OR `days before the hearing, ending 7 clear days before, by which the person charged served on the prosecutor a written notice identifying or assisting in the identification of the other person`
    OR `the court gave permission`

§ `s 57 Powers of search and seizure`

-- src:4953 | 57.—(1) Any police officer not below the rank of sergeant or any
-- src:4954 | employee authorised by the Authority may, if he or she has
-- src:4955 | reasonable grounds for believing that a telecommunication system
-- src:4956 | or service has been established, installed, maintained, operated or
-- src:4957 | provided in contravention of this Act or any regulations made under
-- src:4958 | this Act or in breach of any licence granted by the Authority or that
-- src:4959 | any telecommunication equipment used is of a type that is not
-- src:4960 | approved by the Authority under section 11 or that the
-- src:4961 | telecommunication equipment is imported in contravention of any
-- src:4962 | of the provisions of this Act or any regulations made under this Act —
@ref s 57(1) opening words (src:4953-4962)
GIVEN `the officer is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an employee authorised by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that a telecommunication system or service has been established, installed, maintained, operated or provided in contravention of this Act or its regulations or in breach of a licence granted by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that telecommunication equipment used is of a type not approved by the Authority under section 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that the telecommunication equipment is imported in contravention of this Act or its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(1): the officer has the power conferred by paragraphs (a) and (b)` MEANS
        `the officer is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an employee authorised by the Authority`
    AND (   `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that a telecommunication system or service has been established, installed, maintained, operated or provided in contravention of this Act or its regulations or in breach of a licence granted by the Authority`
         OR `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that telecommunication equipment used is of a type not approved by the Authority under section 11`
         OR `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that the telecommunication equipment is imported in contravention of this Act or its regulations`)

-- src:4964 | (a) in the case of any telecommunication equipment or any
-- src:4965 | telecommunication system or service, other than any
-- src:4966 | radio‑communication system or service, enter and
-- src:4967 | inspect any place in which the telecommunication
-- src:4968 | equipment is located or the telecommunication system or
-- src:4969 | service is established, installed, maintained, operated or
-- src:4970 | provided, and may seize any telecommunication system or
-- src:4971 | equipment found therein which appears to be used for or in
-- src:4972 | connection with telecommunications; and
-- src:4974 | (b) in the case of any radio‑communication system or service,
-- src:4975 | enter any place in Singapore or stop or board any vessel,
-- src:4976 | aircraft or vehicle and inspect any place therein and may
-- src:4977 | seize any radio‑communication system or equipment
-- src:4978 | found therein which appears to be used or is capable of
-- src:4979 | being used for or in connection with
-- src:4980 | radio‑communications.
@ref s 57(1)(a) and (b) (src:4964-4980)
GIVEN `the officer has the power under the opening words of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment, system or service is a radio-communication system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(1)(a): the officer may enter and inspect the place and seize the telecommunication system or equipment found there which appears to be used for or in connection with telecommunications` MEANS
    `the officer has the power under the opening words of subsection (1)` AND (NOT `the equipment, system or service is a radio-communication system or service`)

GIVEN `the officer has the power under the opening words of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment, system or service is a radio-communication system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment found appears to be used, or is capable of being used, for or in connection with radio-communications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(1)(b): the officer may enter any place in Singapore, or stop or board a vessel, aircraft or vehicle, inspect any place in it, and seize the radio-communication system or equipment found` MEANS
    `the officer has the power under the opening words of subsection (1)` AND `the equipment, system or service is a radio-communication system or service` AND `the equipment found appears to be used, or is capable of being used, for or in connection with radio-communications`

-- src:4985 | (2) Where any police officer not below the rank of sergeant or any
-- src:4986 | employee authorised by the Authority has reasonable grounds for
-- src:4987 | believing that an offence has been or is being committed under
-- src:4988 | section 53, 54, 55, 59 or 64, he or she may seize any
-- src:4989 | telecommunication system or equipment or any
-- src:4990 | radio‑communication system or equipment, or any other thing used
-- src:4991 | in the commission of the offence.
@ref s 57(2) (src:4985-4991)
GIVEN `the officer is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an employee authorised by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section of the offence the officer believes has been or is being committed` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(2): the officer may seize any telecommunication or radio-communication system or equipment, or any other thing used in the commission of the offence` MEANS
    `the officer is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an employee authorised by the Authority` AND elem `the section of the offence the officer believes has been or is being committed` (LIST "53", "54", "55", "59", "64")

-- src:4998 | (4) Any person asserting that the person is the owner of the
-- src:4999 | equipment or system may personally or by the person’s authorised
-- src:5000 | agent give written notice to the Authority that the person claims the
-- src:5001 | same.
@ref s 57(4) (src:4998-5001)
GIVEN `the person asserts being the owner of the equipment or system and gives written notice to the Authority, personally or by an authorised agent, that the person claims it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(4): the person has made a claim` MEANS
    `the person asserts being the owner of the equipment or system and gives written notice to the Authority, personally or by an authorised agent, that the person claims it`

-- src:5003 | (5) On receipt of the notice, the Authority may direct that the
-- src:5004 | equipment or system be released or may refer the matter to a
-- src:5005 | Magistrate’s Court or a District Court.
@ref s 57(5) (src:5003-5005)
GIVEN `the Authority received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority directs release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority refers the matter to a Magistrate's Court or a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(5): the Authority has dealt with the claim as the subsection allows` MEANS
    `the Authority received the notice` AND (`the Authority directs release` OR `the Authority refers the matter to a Magistrate's Court or a District Court`)

-- src:5007 | (6) The Magistrate’s Court or the District Court may proceed to the
-- src:5008 | examination of the matter and upon examination shall order that the
-- src:5009 | equipment or system be forfeited or released.
@ref s 57(6) (src:5007-5009)
GIVEN `the matter was referred and the court proceeded to examine it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(6): the court must order that the equipment or system be forfeited or released` MEANS
    `the matter was referred and the court proceeded to examine it`

§ `s 58(1): sealing`

-- src:5015 | 58.—(1) Where it appears to any police officer not below the rank
-- src:5016 | of sergeant or any employee authorised by the Authority that it is not
-- src:5017 | practicable to remove from where it is found any telecommunication
-- src:5018 | system or equipment or any radio‑communication system or
-- src:5019 | equipment seized by him or her under section 57 by reason of its
-- src:5020 | nature, size or amount, he or she may by any means seal the
-- src:5021 | telecommunication system or equipment or the radio‑communication
-- src:5022 | system or equipment.
@ref s 58(1) (src:5015-5022)
GIVEN `the officer is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an employee authorised by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not practicable to remove from where it is found the system or equipment seized under section 57, by reason of its nature, size or amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58(1): the officer may by any means seal the system or equipment` MEANS
    `the officer is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or an employee authorised by the Authority` AND `it is not practicable to remove from where it is found the system or equipment seized under section 57, by reason of its nature, size or amount`

§ `ss 60 to 63: obstruction, damage, divulging messages, fraudulent use`

-- src:5053 | 60.—(1) Any person who —
-- src:5055 | (a) while in any premises used for the purposes of the business
-- src:5056 | of a public telecommunication licensee, intentionally
-- src:5057 | obstructs the course of business of the licensee
-- src:5058 | concerned; or
-- src:5060 | (b) assaults or intentionally obstructs or incites anyone to
-- src:5061 | obstruct or impede an officer or employee of a public
-- src:5062 | telecommunication licensee in the performance of his or
-- src:5063 | her duties,
-- src:5065 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 60(1) (src:5053-5065)
GIVEN `the person, while in premises used for the business of a public telecommunication licensee, intentionally obstructs the course of business of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person assaults, or intentionally obstructs or incites anyone to obstruct or impede, an officer or employee of a public telecommunication licensee in the performance of his or her duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(1): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person, while in premises used for the business of a public telecommunication licensee, intentionally obstructs the course of business of the licensee` OR `the person assaults, or intentionally obstructs or incites anyone to obstruct or impede, an officer or employee of a public telecommunication licensee in the performance of his or her duties`

-- src:5067 | (2) A public telecommunication licensee may require any person
-- src:5068 | guilty of an offence under subsection (1) to leave the premises used
-- src:5069 | for the purposes of its business and, if any such offender who is so
-- src:5070 | required refuses or fails to comply with the requirement, he or she
-- src:5071 | may be removed by an employee of the licensee.
@ref s 60(2) (src:5067-5071)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public telecommunication licensee required the person to leave the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person refuses or fails to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(2): an employee of the licensee may remove the person from the premises` MEANS
    `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` AND `the public telecommunication licensee required the person to leave the premises` AND `the person refuses or fails to comply`

-- src:5081 | 61. Any person who intending —
-- src:5083 | (a) to prevent or obstruct the transmission or delivery of any
-- src:5084 | message;
-- src:5086 | (b) to intercept or to acquaint himself or herself with the
-- src:5087 | contents of any message; or
-- src:5089 | (c) to commit mischief,
-- src:5091 | damages, removes, tampers with or touches any installation or plant
-- src:5092 | (or any part of it) used for telecommunications belonging to a public
-- src:5093 | telecommunication licensee or interferes with the
-- src:5094 | radio‑communication service or system of a public
-- src:5095 | telecommunication licensee shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 61 (src:5081-5095)
GIVEN `the person intends to prevent or obstruct the transmission or delivery of a message` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to intercept or to acquaint himself or herself with the contents of a message` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to commit mischief` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person damages, removes, tampers with or touches installation or plant (or any part of it) used for telecommunications belonging to a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person interferes with the radio-communication service or system of a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 61: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        (   `the person intends to prevent or obstruct the transmission or delivery of a message`
         OR `the person intends to intercept or to acquaint himself or herself with the contents of a message`
         OR `the person intends to commit mischief`)
    AND (   `the person damages, removes, tampers with or touches installation or plant (or any part of it) used for telecommunications belonging to a public telecommunication licensee`
         OR `the person interferes with the radio-communication service or system of a public telecommunication licensee`)

-- src:5104 | 62.—(1) Any officer, employee or agent of a public
-- src:5105 | telecommunication licensee who —
-- src:5107 | (a) wilfully divulges, makes away with or alters any message
-- src:5108 | or record of any message; or
-- src:5110 | (b) except in obedience to an order under the hand of the
-- src:5111 | Minister or the direction of a court, wilfully omits to
-- src:5112 | transmit or intercepts or acquaints himself or herself with
-- src:5113 | or detains any message (or part of it) or deliberately causes
-- src:5114 | a call or connection to be disconnected or not to be
-- src:5115 | connected,
-- src:5117 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 62(1) (src:5104-5117)
GIVEN `the person is an officer, employee or agent of a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wilfully divulges, makes away with or alters a message or a record of a message` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, except in obedience to an order under the hand of the Minister or the direction of a court, wilfully omits to transmit, or intercepts, or acquaints himself or herself with, or detains a message or part of one, or deliberately causes a call or connection to be disconnected or not to be connected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 62(1): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person is an officer, employee or agent of a public telecommunication licensee` AND (`the person wilfully divulges, makes away with or alters a message or a record of a message` OR `the person, except in obedience to an order under the hand of the Minister or the direction of a court, wilfully omits to transmit, or intercepts, or acquaints himself or herself with, or detains a message or part of one, or deliberately causes a call or connection to be disconnected or not to be connected`)

-- src:5121 | (2) Subsection (1)(b) does not apply to —
-- src:5123 | (a) any act or thing done by an officer, employee or agent of a
-- src:5124 | public telecommunication licensee for or in connection
-- src:5125 | with the installation of a telecommunication line,
-- src:5127 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5128 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 104
-- src:5130 | equipment or the operation or maintenance of a
-- src:5131 | telecommunication system; or
-- src:5133 | (b) the tracing of the origin of any telephone call at the request
-- src:5134 | of the subscriber of a telecommunication service.
@ref s 62(2) (src:5121-5134)
GIVEN `the act or thing is done for or in connection with the installation of a telecommunication line, equipment or the operation or maintenance of a telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the tracing of the origin of a telephone call at the request of the subscriber of a telecommunication service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 62(2): subsection (1)(b) does not apply to the act` MEANS
    `the act or thing is done for or in connection with the installation of a telecommunication line, equipment or the operation or maintenance of a telecommunication system` OR `the act is the tracing of the origin of a telephone call at the request of the subscriber of a telecommunication service`

-- src:5139 | 63. Any person who dishonestly uses or permits another person to
-- src:5140 | use any telecommunication service provided by a telecommunication
-- src:5141 | licensee with intent to avoid payment of any charge applicable to the
-- src:5142 | provision of that service shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 63 (src:5139-5142)
GIVEN `the person dishonestly uses, or permits another person to use, a telecommunication service provided by a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to avoid payment of a charge applicable to the provision of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person dishonestly uses, or permits another person to use, a telecommunication service provided by a telecommunication licensee` AND `the person intends to avoid payment of a charge applicable to the provision of the service`

§ `s 64(3), (4): supplying a thing for a fraudulent purpose`

-- src:5173 | (3) Subsection (4) applies if a person supplies or offers to supply
-- src:5174 | any thing which may be used for the purpose of obtaining, or for a
-- src:5175 | purpose connected with the obtaining of, a service to which
-- src:5176 | section 63 applies.
-- src:5178 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5179 | 105 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:5181 | (4) If the person (called in this subsection the supplier) supplying or
-- src:5182 | offering to supply the thing mentioned in subsection (3) knows or
-- src:5183 | believes that the person to whom it is supplied or offered intends or
-- src:5184 | intends if it is supplied to the person —
-- src:5186 | (a) to use the thing —
-- src:5188 | (i) to obtain such a service dishonestly; or
-- src:5190 | (ii) for a purpose connected with the dishonest obtaining
-- src:5191 | of such a service;
-- src:5193 | (b) dishonestly to allow the thing to be used for a purpose
-- src:5194 | connected with the dishonest obtaining of such a service;
-- src:5195 | or
-- src:5197 | (c) to allow the thing to be used for a purpose connected with
-- src:5198 | the dishonest obtaining of such a service,
-- src:5200 | the supplier shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 64(3) and (4) (src:5173-5200)
GIVEN `the person supplies or offers to supply a thing which may be used for obtaining, or for a purpose connected with obtaining, a service to which section 63 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supplier knows or believes that the person supplied or offered intends, or intends if it is supplied, to use the thing to obtain such a service dishonestly or for a purpose connected with the dishonest obtaining of such a service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supplier knows or believes that the person supplied or offered intends dishonestly to allow the thing to be used for a purpose connected with the dishonest obtaining of such a service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supplier knows or believes that the person supplied or offered intends to allow the thing to be used for a purpose connected with the dishonest obtaining of such a service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(4): the supplier is guilty of an offence` MEANS
        `the person supplies or offers to supply a thing which may be used for obtaining, or for a purpose connected with obtaining, a service to which section 63 applies`
    AND (   `the supplier knows or believes that the person supplied or offered intends, or intends if it is supplied, to use the thing to obtain such a service dishonestly or for a purpose connected with the dishonest obtaining of such a service`
         OR `the supplier knows or believes that the person supplied or offered intends dishonestly to allow the thing to be used for a purpose connected with the dishonest obtaining of such a service`
         OR `the supplier knows or believes that the person supplied or offered intends to allow the thing to be used for a purpose connected with the dishonest obtaining of such a service`)

§ `ss 65 to 70`

-- src:5210 | 65. Any person who —
-- src:5212 | (a) fraudulently retains or wilfully divulges, makes away with
-- src:5213 | or detains a message or record of a message which ought to
-- src:5214 | have been delivered to some other person; or
-- src:5216 | (b) being required by a public telecommunication licensee to
-- src:5217 | deliver up any such message or record of such message
-- src:5218 | neglects or refuses to do so,
-- src:5220 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 65 (src:5210-5220)
GIVEN `the person fraudulently retains, or wilfully divulges, makes away with or detains, a message or record of a message which ought to have been delivered to some other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was required by a public telecommunication licensee to deliver up such a message or record and neglects or refuses to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person fraudulently retains, or wilfully divulges, makes away with or detains, a message or record of a message which ought to have been delivered to some other person` OR `the person was required by a public telecommunication licensee to deliver up such a message or record and neglects or refuses to do so`

-- src:5228 | 66.—(1) A person must not, without the written approval of the
-- src:5229 | Authority —
-- src:5231 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5232 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 106
-- src:5234 | (a) lay or carry any mains, pipes, conduits, circuits or wires in,
-- src:5235 | along, through, across, over or under any street or place in
-- src:5236 | a manner which is likely to interfere with or cause damage
-- src:5237 | to any installation or plant used for telecommunications; or
-- src:5239 | (b) affix any placard, advertisement, notice or other thing in or
-- src:5240 | on, or paint, tar or in any way disfigure any installation or
-- src:5241 | plant used for telecommunications.
@ref s 66(1) (src:5228-5241)
GIVEN `the person has the written approval of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person lays or carries mains, pipes, conduits, circuits or wires in, along, through, across, over or under a street or place in a manner likely to interfere with or cause damage to installation or plant used for telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person affixes a placard, advertisement, notice or other thing in or on, or paints, tars or in any way disfigures, installation or plant used for telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(1): the person contravenes the subsection` MEANS
    (NOT `the person has the written approval of the Authority`) AND (`the person lays or carries mains, pipes, conduits, circuits or wires in, along, through, across, over or under a street or place in a manner likely to interfere with or cause damage to installation or plant used for telecommunications` OR `the person affixes a placard, advertisement, notice or other thing in or on, or paints, tars or in any way disfigures, installation or plant used for telecommunications`)

-- src:5243 | (2) Any approval under subsection (1) may be refused by the
-- src:5244 | Authority or granted by the Authority on such terms and conditions as
-- src:5245 | it may determine.
@ref s 66(2) (src:5243-5245)
GIVEN `the Authority refuses or grants the approval on terms and conditions it determines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2): the Authority may refuse the approval or grant it on such terms and conditions as it determines` MEANS
    `the Authority refuses or grants the approval on terms and conditions it determines`

-- src:5247 | (3) Where the commission by any person of an offence under
-- src:5248 | subsection (1) is due to the act or default of some other person, that
-- src:5249 | other person shall be guilty of the offence; and a person may be
-- src:5250 | charged with and convicted of the offence by virtue of this subsection
-- src:5251 | whether or not proceedings are taken against the firstmentioned
-- src:5252 | person.
@ref s 66(3) (src:5247-5252)
GIVEN `the commission of the offence under subsection (1) is due to the act or default of some other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(3): that other person is guilty of the offence, whether or not proceedings are taken against the first person` MEANS
    `the commission of the offence under subsection (1) is due to the act or default of some other person`

-- src:5254 | (4) In any proceedings for an offence under subsection (1), it is,
-- src:5255 | subject to subsection (5), a defence for the person charged to prove
-- src:5256 | that the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due
-- src:5257 | diligence to avoid committing the offence.
-- src:5259 | (5) Where the defence provided by subsection (4) involves an
-- src:5260 | allegation that the commission of the offence was due to the act or
-- src:5261 | default of another person, the person charged is not, without
-- src:5262 | permission of the court, entitled to rely on that defence unless,
-- src:5263 | within a period ending 7 clear days before the hearing, the person
-- src:5264 | charged has served on the prosecutor a written notice giving such
-- src:5265 | information identifying or assisting in the identification of that other
-- src:5266 | person as was then in the possession of the person charged.
@ref s 66(4) and (5) (src:5254-5266)
GIVEN `the person proves that the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defence involves an allegation that the offence was due to the act or default of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written notice identifying or assisting in the identification of the other person was served on the prosecutor within a period ending 7 clear days before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(4) and (5): the person charged may rely on the defence` MEANS
    `the person proves that the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence`
    AND ((NOT `the defence involves an allegation that the offence was due to the act or default of another person`) OR `a written notice identifying or assisting in the identification of the other person was served on the prosecutor within a period ending 7 clear days before the hearing` OR `the court gave permission`)

-- src:5270 | (6) Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with
-- src:5271 | subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence and shall, in addition to
-- src:5272 | the forfeiture of any equipment seized, be liable on conviction to a
-- src:5273 | fine not exceeding $10,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- src:5274 | a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:5275 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 66(6) (src:5270-5275)
GIVEN `the person contravenes or fails to comply with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 66(6): the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person contravenes or fails to comply with subsection (1)` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 10000, 0, 1000, TRUE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5285 | 67. Any person who, without the permission of a public
-- src:5286 | telecommunication licensee, places or maintains in or on any house
-- src:5287 | or place, belonging to or under the control of the person, any word,
-- src:5288 | letter or mark which signifies or implies or may reasonably lead the
-- src:5289 | public to believe that the house or place is part of a public
-- src:5290 | telecommunication licensee’s installation or plant shall be guilty of
-- src:5291 | an offence.
@ref s 67 (src:5285-5291)
GIVEN `the person has the permission of a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person places or maintains in or on a house or place belonging to or under the control of the person a word, letter or mark which signifies or implies, or may reasonably lead the public to believe, that the house or place is part of a public telecommunication licensee's installation or plant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 67: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    (NOT `the person has the permission of a public telecommunication licensee`) AND `the person places or maintains in or on a house or place belonging to or under the control of the person a word, letter or mark which signifies or implies, or may reasonably lead the public to believe, that the house or place is part of a public telecommunication licensee's installation or plant`

-- src:5298 | 68.—(1) Any person who wilfully removes, destroys or damages
-- src:5299 | any installation or plant used for telecommunications shall be guilty
-- src:5300 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:5301 | $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to
-- src:5302 | both.
@ref s 68(1) (src:5298-5302)
GIVEN `the person wilfully removes, destroys or damages installation or plant used for telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 68(1): the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person wilfully removes, destroys or damages installation or plant used for telecommunications` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 50000, 36, 0, FALSE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5304 | (2) Despite subsection (1), any person who, in the course of
-- src:5305 | carrying out any earthworks, damages or suffers to be damaged any
-- src:5306 | cable of a telecommunication system belonging to or under the
-- src:5307 | management or control of a telecommunication system licensee shall
-- src:5308 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:5309 | exceeding $1 million or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:5310 | 5 years or to both.
@ref s 68(2) (src:5304-5310)
GIVEN `the person, in the course of carrying out earthworks, damages or suffers to be damaged a cable of a telecommunication system belonging to or under the management or control of a telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 68(2): the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person, in the course of carrying out earthworks, damages or suffers to be damaged a cable of a telecommunication system belonging to or under the management or control of a telecommunication system licensee` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 1000000, 60, 0, FALSE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5312 | (3) Where an offence under subsection (2) is committed by any
-- src:5313 | person (called in this subsection the firstmentioned person) acting as
-- src:5314 | the agent or employee of another person (called in this subsection the
-- src:5315 | principal person), or being otherwise subject to the supervision or
-- src:5316 | instructions of another person (also called in this subsection the
-- src:5317 | principal person) for the purposes of any employment in the course of
-- src:5318 | which the offence was committed, the principal person shall, without
-- src:5319 | prejudice to the liability of the firstmentioned person, be liable under
-- src:5320 | that subsection in the same manner and to the same extent as if the
-- src:5321 | principal person had personally committed the offence unless the
-- src:5322 | principal person proves to the satisfaction of the court that the offence
-- src:5323 | was committed without the principal person’s consent or connivance
-- src:5325 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5326 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 108
-- src:5328 | or that it was not attributable to any neglect on the principal person’s
-- src:5329 | part.
@ref s 68(3) (src:5312-5329)
GIVEN `the offence under subsection (2) was committed by a person acting as the agent or employee of, or subject to the supervision or instructions of, another person in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal person proves to the satisfaction of the court that the offence was committed without the principal person's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal person proves to the satisfaction of the court that the offence was not attributable to any neglect on the principal person's part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(3): the principal person is liable under subsection (2) as if the principal person had personally committed the offence` MEANS
    `the offence under subsection (2) was committed by a person acting as the agent or employee of, or subject to the supervision or instructions of, another person in the course of employment` AND (NOT (`the principal person proves to the satisfaction of the court that the offence was committed without the principal person's consent or connivance` OR `the principal person proves to the satisfaction of the court that the offence was not attributable to any neglect on the principal person's part`))

-- src:5331 | (4) In any proceedings for an offence under subsection (2), it is a
-- src:5332 | defence for the person charged to prove that the person took all
-- src:5333 | reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid the
-- src:5334 | commission of the offence.
@ref s 68(4) (src:5331-5334)
GIVEN `the person charged proves that the person took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(4): the person charged has a defence to the offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the person charged proves that the person took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence`

-- src:5336 | (5) If in any proceedings for an offence under subsection (2) the
-- src:5337 | defence involves acting on information supplied by a
-- src:5338 | telecommunication system licensee or a licensed
-- src:5339 | telecommunication cable detection worker, the person charged is
-- src:5340 | not, without permission of the court, entitled to rely on that defence
-- src:5341 | unless, within a period of 14 clear days before the hearing, the person
-- src:5342 | has served on the prosecutor a written notice giving such information
-- src:5343 | as was then in the person’s possession identifying or assisting in the
-- src:5344 | identification of the telecommunication system licensee or
-- src:5345 | telecommunication cable detection worker.
@ref s 68(5) (src:5336-5345)
GIVEN `the defence involves acting on information supplied by a telecommunication system licensee or a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written notice identifying or assisting in the identification of the licensee or worker was served on the prosecutor within a period of 14 clear days before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(5): the person charged may rely on the defence` MEANS
    (NOT `the defence involves acting on information supplied by a telecommunication system licensee or a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker`) OR `a written notice identifying or assisting in the identification of the licensee or worker was served on the prosecutor within a period of 14 clear days before the hearing` OR `the court gave permission`

-- src:5354 | 69.—(1) Any person who removes, destroys or damages, whether
-- src:5355 | wilfully, negligently, accidentally or otherwise, the installation or
-- src:5356 | plant used for telecommunications is, in addition to any penalty for
-- src:5357 | which the person is liable for an offence under this Act, liable to pay
-- src:5358 | compensation for the damage the person has done and the
-- src:5359 | compensation is recoverable by civil action or suit before any court
-- src:5360 | of competent jurisdiction.
@ref s 69(1) (src:5354-5360)
GIVEN `the person removes, destroys or damages, whether wilfully, negligently, accidentally or otherwise, installation or plant used for telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 69(1): the person is liable to pay compensation for the damage, recoverable by civil action, in addition to any penalty` MEANS
    `the person removes, destroys or damages, whether wilfully, negligently, accidentally or otherwise, installation or plant used for telecommunications`

-- src:5362 | (2) Subject to subsection (1), any court before which a person is
-- src:5363 | charged with an offence under this Act may assess the compensation
-- src:5364 | payable under this section and may make an order for the payment of
-- src:5365 | the same.
@ref s 69(2) (src:5362-5365)
GIVEN `the person is charged before the court with an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 69(2): the court may assess the compensation payable and make an order for payment` MEANS
    `the person is charged before the court with an offence under the Act`

-- src:5367 | (3) Any order under subsection (2) may be enforced as if it were a
-- src:5368 | judgment in a civil action or suit.
@ref s 69(3) (src:5367-5368)
GIVEN `the order is made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 69(3): the order may be enforced as if it were a judgment in a civil action or suit` MEANS
    `the order is made under subsection (2)`

-- src:5378 | 70.—(1) Any person who, with fraudulent intent, erases or removes
-- src:5379 | from any device, any mark put or impressed upon the device denoting
-- src:5380 | that the same has been used, or sells or uses any such device shall be
-- src:5381 | guilty of an offence.
@ref s 70(1) (src:5378-5381)
GIVEN `the person, with fraudulent intent, erases or removes from a device a mark put or impressed upon it denoting that it has been used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, with fraudulent intent, sells or uses such a device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70(1): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person, with fraudulent intent, erases or removes from a device a mark put or impressed upon it denoting that it has been used` OR `the person, with fraudulent intent, sells or uses such a device`

-- src:5385 | (2) In this section, “device” means any device provided for use by a
-- src:5386 | public telecommunication licensee for accessing any
-- src:5387 | telecommunication equipment of the licensee to enable the
-- src:5388 | telecommunication service of the licensee to be used.
@ref s 70(2) (src:5385-5388)
GIVEN `it is a device provided for use by a public telecommunication licensee for accessing telecommunication equipment of the licensee to enable its telecommunication service to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70(2): this is a "device"` MEANS
    `it is a device provided for use by a public telecommunication licensee for accessing telecommunication equipment of the licensee to enable its telecommunication service to be used`
